{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119097","id":3604798974,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc7W3N3-","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119097","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119097.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119097.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119097","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119097/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119097/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119097/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/698a052e9700704d2eab9de2fcb2d4cea66a8117","number":119097,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Fix issue with constant editor redraw if any Joint3D derived node exists in scene","user":{"login":"fLindahl","id":18470258,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NDcwMjU4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18470258?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fLindahl","html_url":"https://github.com/fLindahl","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fLindahl/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fLindahl/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fLindahl/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fLindahl/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fLindahl/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fLindahl/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fLindahl/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fLindahl/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fLindahl/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Instead of lazily just redrawing every now and then, instead we check for a couple of specific conditions:\r\n\r\n1. The joint node has moved (notification TRANSFORM_CHANGED)\r\n2. Node A or B has been changed in the joint.\r\n3. Node A or B has been moved since last update. This is currently done via polling and keeping track of the last known positional state, which isn't optimal, but better than letting the editor constantly redraw.\r\n\r\nTo keep track of each gizmos individual a/b nodes previous positions, I added a `register_gizmo` method to `EditorNode3DGizmo` (already had a deregister method) and made them virtual so that we can hook in and react to when gizmos are added/removed.\r\n\r\nIn the end, this avoids redrawing unnecessarily. We noticed this as the spinner kept spinning constantly, and we also realized that we had better performance when running our game if the viewport wasn't opened in the editor (e.g. script tab was opened instead), which is probably the most important reason for this fix.\r\n\r\nIt still has a timer set to 120hz, that updates a single gizmo per \"tick\", effectively amortizing the cost of polling for changes. It's not pretty, but I couldn't find a better way to listen to \"external\" node transform changes.\r\n\r\nTest project:\r\n[joint-3d-redraw-fix.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/27216650/joint-3d-redraw-fix.zip)\r\n","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098219,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgyMTk=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:editor","name":"topic:editor","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":370471880,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzNzA0NzE4ODA=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:physics","name":"topic:physics","description":"","color":"ffee88","d